Item 05 is done and marked `[x]`; the gate passed; nothing is left running.

**What was done.** The contraction-minor search of item 04 was taken to scale in `learning/obstruction_minor.py`: an output-directory switch, C caps and budgets by size, a core-hour scheduler, a `ridge` stage, node counts in every certificate, and the checker extended to the ladder's certificate where it is the better one. 185 instances were run (107 at 61–134 customers, 78 Chu & Stuckey at 30–50) and the 22 Chu & Stuckey gap instances item 04 ran were carried in, giving the 207 distinct targets. Six tests were added. The report has §5; PROGRESS has the iteration entry.

**Findings.**
- Family M's floor is tight on 73 of the 87 gap instances above 60 customers and on 186 of the 200 Chu & Stuckey instances. With the record, 327 of the 338 are closed and 11 open, all dense 100- and 125-customer instances on the ridge's dense shoulder.
- M is at least as tight as family E on every one of the 200, tighter on 142. The record's expectation that expansion wins on dense classes holds only at density 10, where the two tie.
- The search beats the ladder on 60 of 185, on 41 of them with a minor above 95% of the vertices. The ladder's grid stops at 95%, so most of its shortfall on dense instances is a grid artefact. A 97–99% rung is proposed, not applied.
- `Random-125-125-2-3_0` now has a 51-vertex certificate refuting 19 in 145,355 nodes and 0.12 s, rule-free verified, against the record's 70 vertices.
- `Random-125-125-2-2_0`: no certificate for 25 under one core-hour. 55 C calls at 97–110 vertices, all undecided or proved useless. A recorded negative, not a kill.
- Checker: 190 of 190 verified. Harness: above optimum 0 on all 6,376.

**Kill verdict.** Not met: the search beats the ladder on 45 of the 338 (13.3%).

**Compute.** About 10.6 core-hours of the item's 22; no instance was cut by the 18-core-hour stop.

**One slip, repaired.** The module's log path was bound at import time, so the main run logged into item 04's log. The default is now resolved at call time, item 05's log was rebuilt from the stdout captures, and item 04's was restored from git.

**Next.** Item 06, family B on the 11 residual gap instances.

